{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OptiViewAdsCore"}],"externalID":"s:15OptiViewAdsCore09PictureInE7CapableP","symbolKind":"protocol","title":"PictureInPictureCapable","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PictureInPictureCapable","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PictureInPictureCapable","kind":"identifier"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Player contract","identifiers":["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapterEvent","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/TimedMetadataCue","doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/ContentVideoSizeProvider"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Player-contract"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PictureInPictureCapable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : AnyObject","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The runtime’s default is to drive ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVPictureInPictureController"},{"text":" against the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"content ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AVPlayerLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" it discovers in the integrator’s view hierarchy."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That works for players that keep one layer alive across source changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(AVPlayer: the SDK swaps the ITEM on the same player), and breaks for"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"players that rebuild their internal pipeline on a source change: THEOplayer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"replaces its internal AVPlayer\/layer when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source"},{"text":" is assigned, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discovered layer dies, and AVKit closes the window at the exact moment the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SDK lends the content player to the ad. Measured on the iOS e2e fleet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(catalog-pip, SDK 0.50.0-beta.500): the window opened before the break and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closed at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adbreakbegin"},{"text":", with the ad playing full-screen in the main","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window instead of inside it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Such players expose their own picture-in-picture facility with the missing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"piece — THEOplayer retains the window across source changes when the host","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constructs it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PiPConfiguration(retainPresentationModeOnSourceChange: true)"},{"text":" — but only if the window is driven through THAT facility. This","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol is how an adapter hands the SDK that steering wheel; the renderer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prefers it over its own controller whenever the content adapter conforms.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All three members are called on the